<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 3 April, from 956 to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">956 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,070 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Polyeuctus is elected Patriarch of Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Polyeuctus was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecumenical-patriarch-of-constantinople">Ecumenical Patriarch of Constantinople</a>, archbishop of the city and senior <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Eastern Orthodox Church</a>, and held the office until 970. His feast in the Orthodox Church is on 5 February.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecumenical-patriarch-of-constantinople">Ecumenical Patriarch of Constantinople</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1043 CE <span class="tih-ago">983 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward the Confessor is crowned king at Winchester</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor">Edward the Confessor</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-the-unready">Æthelred the Unready</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emma-of-normandy">Emma of Normandy</a>, was crowned king of the English in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a> Cathedral, having succeeded his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harthacnut">Harthacnut</a> in 1042. He was the last reigning monarch of the House of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor">Edward the Confessor</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1367">1367 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">659 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Black Prince defeats Henry of Trastámara at Nájera</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-black-prince">Edward the Black Prince</a> routed the Castilian and French army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-castile">Henry of Trastámara</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najera">Nájera</a>, restoring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-castile">Peter of Castile</a>. The victory proved short-lived: Henry killed Peter and took the throne two years later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1559">1559 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">467 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peace of Cateau-Cambrésis ends the Italian Wars</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> signed the treaty that closed more than sixty years of war over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, a day after a separate Anglo-French peace. Spanish dominance in Italy was confirmed for over a century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1783">1783 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sweden signs a treaty of amity with the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-franklin">Benjamin Franklin</a> and the Swedish envoy Gustaf Philip Creutz signed a treaty of amity and commerce in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> became the first state not at war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to recognise American independence by treaty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1860">1860 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">166 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pony Express sets off on its first run</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Riders left St Joseph, Missouri, and Sacramento, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, carrying mail across some 3,000 km in about ten days. The relay lasted only 18 months before the transcontinental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">telegraph</a> made it obsolete.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1882">1882 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">144 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Ford shoots outlaw Jesse James in Missouri</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jesse James was shot dead at his home in St Joseph by Robert Ford, a member of his own gang hoping for a reward. The killing turned the train and bank robber into an enduring figure of American folklore.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1933">1933 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British biplanes make the first flight over Everest</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two Westland aircraft of the Houston expedition flew over the summit of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-everest">Mount Everest</a>, crews breathing bottled oxygen in open cockpits. They brought back the first aerial photographs of the peak.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Martin Luther King gives his 'Mountaintop' speech</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Memphis, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther-king-jr">Martin Luther King Jr.</a> told supporters he had 'seen the Promised Land' but might not get there with them. It was his last speech; he was assassinated the following evening.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 3 April <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-xingzong-of-liao"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Emperor Xingzong of Liao</span><span class="tp">1016–1055</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/theodoros-kolokotronis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/theodoros-kolokotronis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Theodoros Kolokotronis</span><span class="tp">1770–1843</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/arturo-prat"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/arturo-prat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Arturo Prat</span><span class="tp">1848–1879</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tomas-bata"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tomas-bata.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tomáš Baťa</span><span class="tp">1876–1932</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alcide-de-gasperi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alcide-de-gasperi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alcide De Gasperi</span><span class="tp">1881–1954</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/helmut-kohl"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/helmut-kohl.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Helmut Kohl</span><span class="tp">1930–2017</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/carlos-salinas-de-gortari"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/carlos-salinas-de-gortari.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Carlos Salinas de Gortari</span><span class="tp">b. 1948</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 3 April <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-iii-duke-of-aquitaine"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">William III, Duke of Aquitaine</span><span class="tp">c. 915–963</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nizamuddin-auliya"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nizamuddin-auliya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nizamuddin Auliya</span><span class="tp">1238–1325</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/shivaji"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/shivaji.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Shivaji</span><span class="tp">1630–1680</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bartolome-esteban-murillo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bartolome-esteban-murillo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bartolomé Esteban Murillo</span><span class="tp">1617–1682</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-pocock"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-pocock.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Pocock</span><span class="tp">1706–1792</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johannes-brahms"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johannes-brahms.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johannes Brahms</span><span class="tp">1833–1897</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
